          {
            "id": 1905,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Overall",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"WC9GdWptxodM3rxqUu4lYwk6gDd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-KPTtdEOOEozWvFxZdNrl28kIgyb\">Overall, the process consists of eight stages to create a storage area from concrete canvas. The procedure begins with the manufacturing of concrete canvas, involves delivery and installation steps, and ends with a functional storage facility that is ready for use.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 18719,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 1906,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"WC9GdWptxodM3rxqUu4lYwk6gDd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-IRDydFTtto9ESwxXXanlJ71LgFd\">The process commences with manufacturing, where concrete canvas is produced using three layers: a fibrous top surface, dry concrete, and a waterproof layer at the bottom. Subsequently, the material is delivered to the construction site by truck, with a cover used to prevent dust. In the third stage, the concrete canvas is unwrapped and prepared for installation. The canvas is then spread out on the ground creating a flat surface that measures approximately 10 meters in length, using pegs and ropes to secure stability.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 18719,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 1907,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"WC9GdWptxodM3rxqUu4lYwk6gDd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-Ay9hdjP67o4HvCxP5fZldH7jgVh\">Following the initial setup, air is pumped into the concrete canvas structure through a door mechanism, causing it to inflate and take the shape of a storage unit. The next crucial step involves watering the entire surface, which activates the concrete material within the canvas. The structure then requires a setting period of 20-24 hours to allow the concrete to harden and solidify. Finally, once the setting process is complete, the concrete canvas storage area is ready for use and can accommodate various storage needs.</div>\n</div>",
